Model balancing - matlab code
=============================

Installation instructions, requirements, and a quick-start guide
can be found in the file README.md (section "Installation").

In short:

  1. Clone this repository and the toolboxes
       matlab-utils               (https://github.com/liebermeister/matlab-utils)
       metabolic-network-toolbox  (https://github.com/liebermeister/metabolic-network-toolbox)
       sbtab-matlab               (https://github.com/liebermeister/sbtab-matlab)
       enzyme-cost-minimization   (https://github.com/liebermeister/enzyme-cost-minimization)
     and, optionally (only needed for SBML files), the SBML Toolbox
     (https://sbml.org/software/sbmltoolbox/).

  2. Add all these directories, including subdirectories, to your matlab path,
     e.g. addpath(genpath('model-balancing/matlab')).

  3. Run the demo scripts in model-balancing/demo.

The code was tested with Matlab R2019b on Linux.

